    "currentSummary": "WI-V0-01-03 now has a deployed G0-A default-deny training preflight. It accepts only synthetic, value-minimized references; rejects family/proxy subjects, non-eligible subjects, incomplete consent, legacy Provider speaker IDs, raw audio/URL fields and replayed request hashes; and always reports zero Provider effect, SampleObject creation and training-command creation. G0-B adds an iOS optional authority adapter that parses only the authority child of Digital Human session, voice-profile and synthesis contracts; nil, subject mismatch, Vault mismatch and non-blocked status remain default-denied, with no runtime promotion, Provider effect, media parsing or public UI. It does not make M1 Voice ready: real SourceObject binding, scan/retention, Provider training/delete/reconcile and G4 approval remain open.",
