    "interviewSafetyOverrideSummary": "M0A-29 executes SafetyPolicy before formal owner-narrative persistence. Explicit high-risk input returns a value-minimized neutral safety override, writes no interview message or receipt, and leaves the optimistic session version unchanged; normal narrative remains available on the original version. Backend main@4ebeda0 is deployed and isolated Postgres smoke verified this behavior.",
    "atomicDeferEvidence": "../DreamJourneyBackend/docs/backend/2026-07-23-owner-truth-saved-continuation-cue.md",
    "atomicDeferSummary": "f74f18b deploys a default-off Owner QA-only defer-with-continuation route. It accepts only value-free pointers, creates or replays the append-only cue and writes cooldown inside one Postgres UoW, then restores only the same cue after the direct server-observed cooldown transition. Isolated deployed Postgres smoke covers both gates, cross-owner denial, replay, free-text rejection, elapsed recovery and session-version suppression.",
    "cooldownRestoreIOSQAEvidence": "docs/superpowers/status/2026-07-23-wi-s1-01-03-m0a-cooldown-restore-ios-qa.md",
    "cooldownRestoreIOSQASummary": "The existing server-clock-gated restore-cooldown route now has a typed iOS QA consumer. It sends only commandId/threadId/expectedSessionVersion, remains QA transport only, validates AccountLease and generation at request/commit, and Release compiles the UI control out. XCTest and simulator UIQA verify return to active/open without exposing a public Echo route.",
    "sameVaultThreadIsolationEvidence": "../DreamJourneyBackend/docs/backend/2026-07-23-owner-truth-same-vault-thread-isolation.md",
    "sameVaultThreadIsolationSummary": "M0A-31 preserves the existing one-active-session-per-Vault rule. After thread A is paused by cooldown, thread B can start in the same Owner/Vault without inheriting A's preference. Backend rejects session/thread cross-boundary and cross-restore writes with 409; deployed disposable Postgres smoke verifies five valid receipts. iOS uses the same AccountLease for A/B and fails closed if B receives A's receipt: 66 OwnerTruth XCTest cases pass locally. No public control, Memory authority write, Provider call, or release behavior is added.",
    "summary": "The private M0-A interview path is deployed through acknowledged-batch proposal admission, value-minimized review composition, partial acceptance for selected ordinary batch Candidates, individual terminal review for sensitive or explicitly single-review Candidates, a separate default-off iOS QA review consumer, a deployed value-minimized interview-session state read, and a lease-bound typed iOS natural-input client. The existing QA keyboard entry remains double-gated. A product natural-input surface is G0/G1 verified: it starts hidden in the existing full-screen Echo, requires both a fresh route visibility and write decision for echoTextInput, clears immediately on account rebind, and uses product wording without internal QA details. Formal backend writes require a captured server release-policy decision and reject absent policy without falling back to QA. `db95a5f` deployed the input authorization path; `8cb6a0d` deployed a content-free continuation presentation route and its isolated Postgres smoke verified rejected missing capture, matching capture, and presentation semantics without production business-data mutation. The product Sheet maps only server state to a natural summary and never exposes input text, Candidate content, review IDs, pacing, fatigue, or internal session details. Both UIQA surfaces use in-memory clients and never perform a private write, voice turn, or Digital Human request. `79a0504` added a separately policy-gated confirmation read route; iOS has a typed, lease-fenced, default-off read consumer that reuses the captured product policy and never carries the QA header or a decision mutation. `a9efa24` adds the separate formal batch-accept route under the confirmation path: it is default-off, requires a fresh captured `ownerTruthCandidateReview` policy, cannot be bypassed by a QA header, fixes the server-side boundary-confirmation reason, returns no Candidate content or QA receipt envelope, and records terminal Candidate receipts without activating a MemoryVersion. M0A-20 adds a separate typed iOS action consumer for that formal route: it remains fail-closed, validates AccountLease at request and commit, permits only ordinary batch Candidates present in the confirmation projection, rejects single/sensitive Candidate IDs, reuses a command ID for an unchanged retry, rejects QA response envelopes, and discards stale deferred results after account rebind. M0A-21 requires a fresh formal confirmation read after action success and enters confirmed only when every accepted Candidate has disappeared from the refreshed projection; a failed reconciliation preserves the value-minimized action result but does not claim completion. M0A-22 additionally binds a successfully read confirmation projection to the exact AccountLease that passed its completion fence and rejects a reconciliation whose admission/source/version/authority epoch drifts, while allowing candidate membership to change after a decision. `a954ac9` adds hash-minimized formal authorization evidence and immutable root-to-terminal receipt links. `0ab1e73` additionally rejects any populated formal capture whose feature is not `ownerTruthCandidateReview`; migration `0037` is deployed, the database constraint is validated and an online inventory found zero stored non-target captures. `f383e1b` and `179efbd` add a single selected successful ExtractionResult baseline: Candidate review never mixes historical extractions, a newer failed attempt retains the most recent successful pending baseline, and the iOS typed parser rejects mixed responses. `a45170d` deploys the formal owner boundary route, while `07ef43e` adds the lease/generation-fenced iOS use case: it accepts only skipOnce/cooldown/doNotAsk, validates the compatible active/paused receipt lifecycle, refreshes the value-minimized continuation, and discards stale completion after an AccountLease rebind. `5b2bafd` closes the remaining one-shot semantic: the next owner narrative atomically consumes `skipOnce`, its replay retains `open`, and the isolated deployed Postgres smoke verifies the full value-minimized boundary flow. `bc3f055` and `58ec52f` add and deploy M0A-28: a separate, explicitly confirmed restore only for `paused + doNotAsk`, backed by receipt migration `0038`; it rejects cooldown restoration and preserves replay idempotency. `4ebeda0` deploys the crisis safety override. `f74f18b` adds the adjacent default-off atomic “以后再聊” contract: the same Owner QA action stores a value-free continuation cue and starts server-owned cooldown in one UoW, then preserves only that cue across the direct elapsed cooldown transition. It is not public Echo UI, does not add provider input or Candidate/Memory authority writes, and has deployed isolated Postgres evidence. Natural-language topic re-identification and automatic reopening remain intentionally unimplemented pending product matching/ambiguity decisions. Registry status remains deliberately conservative."
